                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.72 AL 5/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-28T19:00:00-05:00">April 28, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 29—12:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Department’s telegram No. 21, April 27, 5 p.m. In reply to my oral request
                    this morning for an extension of 2 weeks, the Minister of Foreign Affairs has
                    just informed me that, in spite of his best efforts, General Enriquez refuses to
                    grant the cable company a greater extension than until Monday, May 2, 5:00
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>Minister Long is presenting his credentials tomorrow morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
